@inproceedings{7724252,
 abstract = {Traditionally agriculture has been India's glory and this work is a step to improve agriculture practices in India with the help of agriculture data analysis. The agriculture data analysis shows 44% approx of agriculture land area cultivates sugarcane crop (2008-09). The yield of the sugarcane is 663.06 quintal approx on average whereas the average yield of the other crop is 21.5. Thus sugarcane is the king of all the crops for India. This work classifies the crop on two factors : first factor is land area under cultivation and second factor is crop yield.},
